    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Classify this GitHub Issue for the project \"Код-репетитор\" — a web service where a tutor assigns homework and schedules lessons, and students submit homework.\n\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nBody: {{ $json.body }}\n\nTypes:\n- bug: something works incorrectly (error, wrong behavior, crash)\n- task: a question about existing functionality, how to do something\n- feature: a request for a new capability\n- unknown: the author reports a problem or need related to the service, but it is too vague to tell what exactly is wrong or wanted\n- spam: clearly NOT about the service — advertising, random characters, greetings without any request\n\nImportant: if the text complains that something \"doesn't work\", \"is broken\", \"is wrong\" — even without details — it is about the service, so it is unknown (or bug if details are given), NEVER spam. Use spam only when there is no relation to the service at all.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Не сохраняется оценка за ДЗ: ставлю 5, нажимаю «Проверено», оценки нет\" → bug, 0.95\n- \"Как репетитору вернуть ДЗ на доработку?\" → task, 0.9\n- \"Добавьте напоминание об уроке за час\" → feature, 0.9\n- \"Иногда не работает. что-то не так\" → unknown, 0.3\n- \"Привет! asdfgh купите курсы недорого\" → spam, 0.95\n\nconfidence: a number from 0 to 1 showing how sure you are. If the description is short or vague, confidence must be low.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ],
